Choplifter! PCjr -- M10 polish
hardware validation (workset bytes, /ztimer)  ground BROWN

BIOS model byte at F000:FFFE ... FD (IBM PCjr)
int 12h 736 KB, pages on entry CRT=4 CPU=4
  JrConfig: JRCONSYS at 09C4:0000, 64 KB at 1000h (mask F0)
  video pages A=6 B=7
stick 1 x=32 y=25 live; btn=0; INT15 x=0 y=0 CF
axes port 201h; deadzone +/-16/255 around 128; joystick 1 = bits 0,1
Plug joystick 1 (first connector).  Centre, then SPACE on the
title.  C opens calibrate.  Up = thrust, down = descend,
left/right = tilt and translate.  Ctrl-A / Ctrl-V invert X / Y.
Esc on the title quits to DOS.

Flew with blit_rle_m8 + SN76496 + M9 presentation (M10 polish) on pages 6/7.  Sim 20 Hz (every 3 retraces).  Controls: Joystick.  Stick source this run: port 201h.
Measured: 20 sim ticks / 60 retraces in 69 BIOS ticks = 5.27 Hz sim (target 20.00).

WORKSET byte counts (every sim present this run).  Not times.
  sim ticks 20  scrolling 0  static 20
                    min     avg     max
  restore             0     872     976
  rle blit          824     859    1080
  video total      1399    1763    1832
  avg mountain 126  scenery 167  sprites 597
  restore is even-padded dirty-rect fill_rect bytes.
  rle blit is skip-stripped payload (opaque + mixed bytes).
  mountain includes the 320-byte band fill when the ridge
  is repainted.  DESIGN.md section 7 ~3000/~320/~1500/~3000
  is analysis; this table is what this run actually wrote.

ANALYSIS -- M1.LOG rates x avg bytes, not a new hardware total.
  restore  872 B * 2935 ns (fill_rect) = 2559 us
  rle blit 859 B * 4515 ns (movsb)     = 3878 us
  Do not add these into a replacement for section 7's ~26 ms.

ZTIMER one present (restore+draw, HUD not included).
  sim_frame 4  bytes restore 968  blit 830  video 1798
  OVERFLOW -- interval exceeded ~54 ms; count is meaningless.
PASS by eye: BIOS title, then Broderbund / logo / Gorlin /
mission screens (SPACE skips), then chopper on the base pad.
HUD rows 0-7: three 24x8 bubbles, two 5x7 digits each.  F1 or `
toggles debug.  FIRST/SECOND/THIRD SORTIE art at sortie start.
64 rescued: crown overlay then title.  64 killed or third crash:
The End then title.  Esc on play or logos quits to DOS.  No
full-screen copy in the sim loop, no trail, no flicker.
WORKSET byte counts print after every flight.  On hardware add
/ztimer /batch /frames=60 and do not touch the keyboard during
the sample.  Stick 1 analog and SN76496 (port 61h gate) are
the rest of the hardware pass; see docs/M10.md.
